From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] login_manager: no hardware overlays on NVIDIA's display
 driver

With nvidia-drm, Chrome's hardware overlays make page flips time out
("Flip event timeout" in the kernel log) once a Linux app's window is up,
such as Steam's: the display stops updating while the system keeps
running. It is the freeze the set_hw_overlay_strategy_none USE flag works
around on some boards, and the same flag (--enable-hardware-overlays="")
fixes it: with it, Steam opens and runs on the NVIDIA test PC (RTX 20 series, nvidia-open)
without a timeout. A NickelOS image serves any GPU, so the flag follows the
driver that is loaded (/sys/module/nvidia_drm; it loads seconds before ui
starts) instead of a board USE flag.

--- a/login_manager/chrome_setup.cc
+++ b/login_manager/chrome_setup.cc
@@ -450,7 +450,13 @@
 
   // TODO(b/180138001): Remove the following flag when a proper fix for
   // the freeze issue is found.
-  if (builder->UseFlagIsSet("set_hw_overlay_strategy_none")) {
+  // NickelOS: NVIDIA's display driver (nvidia-drm) freezes the screen the
+  // same way: with overlays, page flips time out ("Flip event timeout") as
+  // soon as a Linux app's window is up, and the display stops updating. A
+  // NickelOS image serves any GPU, so this follows the driver that is loaded
+  // rather than the board's USE flags.
+  if (builder->UseFlagIsSet("set_hw_overlay_strategy_none") ||
+      base::PathExists(base::FilePath("/sys/module/nvidia_drm"))) {
     builder->AddArg("--enable-hardware-overlays=\"\"");
   }
 
